{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-remainder-modules","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:remainder-modules","kind":"definition","title":"Remainder modules $O(I)$ and $\\widetilde{O}(I)$","uses":["papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-admissible-system","papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-leading-terms"],"tags":["groebner-basis","module"],"leanRef":"ugb:UGB.UnitalGroebner.RemainderModule","text":"remainder-modules.md","leanSource":"folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/remainder-modules.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:remainder-modules\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> be a commutative ring with unity, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> an <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-algebra which is free as an\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-module and without quasi-zeros, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(B, &#x3C;)</code> an admissible system on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code>, and\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">I \\subseteq A</code> a subset. Define the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-submodule <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">O(I)</code> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> — the\n<strong>remainder module</strong> — to be the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-submodule spanned by the set:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">o(I) := \\{\\lambda\\beta \\mid \\lambda \\in R^*,\\; \\beta \\in B,\\; \\forall h \\in I \\text{ we have } \\LT(h) \\neq \\lambda\\beta\\}</code></pre>\n<p>We also define the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-module <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\widetilde{O}(I)</code> as the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-submodule spanned by\nthe set:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">\\widetilde{o}(I) := B \\setminus \\{\\LM(h) \\mid h \\in I\\}</code></pre>\n<p><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\widetilde{O}(I)</code> is a free <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-module.</p>\n","source":"folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/remainder-modules.md","heading":"Definition","number":"2.2.6"}
